Fix a SIGSEGV in the macOS Open panel when an item has no filesystem path.

FLopenDelegate is the NSOpenSavePanelDelegate FLTK installs whenever the open panel carries a
filter popup. AppKit runs that panel out of process and asks the app to enable items in batches
(-[NSSavePanel(ExportedInterface) requestAppEnabledStateForItems:replyBlock:]), and not every
item it asks about is a plain file URL -- cloud, shared and smart-list rows answer nil to
-[NSURL path]. shouldEnableURL: forwarded that nil to shouldShowFilename:, which sent
fileSystemRepresentation to nil (NULL) and handed the NULL straight to fl_filename_match(), which
dereferences its first argument:

    0  fl_filename_match(char const*, char const*) + 424      <- ldrsb w0, [x19]; x19 = 0
    1  fl_filename_match(char const*, char const*) + 672      <- the 'case *' recursion
    2  -[FLopenDelegate panel:shouldShowFilename:] + 224
    3  -[NSSavePanel(ExportedInterface) requestAppEnabledStateForItems:replyBlock:] + 876

The same line also indexes filter_pattern[] with indexOfSelectedItem unchecked. The popup holds
_filt_total patterns, then a separator, then "All Files", so only 0..numberOfItems-3 are valid
indices; the separator row and the -1 "nothing selected" answer both read out of bounds. Only the
"All Files" row was excluded.

Guard all three: an unusable index, a nil filename, and a NULL pattern or path each mean "no
pattern to test against", so the item is shown -- which is what the popup's own "All Files" row
already does.

Written against FLTK 1.4.5, not yet sent upstream; drop this patch once it lands there.

--- a/src/Fl_Native_File_Chooser_MAC.mm
+++ b/src/Fl_Native_File_Chooser_MAC.mm
@@ -497,11 +497,21 @@
 }
 - (BOOL)panel:(id)sender shouldShowFilename:(NSString *)filename
 {
-  if ( [nspopup indexOfSelectedItem] == [nspopup numberOfItems] - 1) return YES;
+  // The popup holds _filt_total patterns, then a separator, then "All Files": only
+  // 0..numberOfItems-3 index filter_pattern, and indexOfSelectedItem is -1 when nothing is
+  // selected. Anything else means "no pattern to test against", i.e. show the item.
+  NSInteger selected = [nspopup indexOfSelectedItem];
+  if (selected < 0 || selected > [nspopup numberOfItems] - 3) return YES;
+  // The panel runs out of process and asks about items that are not plain file URLs (cloud and
+  // shared rows, smart lists), whose -[NSURL path] is nil -- and so is the filename here.
+  if (filename == nil) return YES;
   BOOL isdir = NO;
   [[NSFileManager defaultManager] fileExistsAtPath:filename isDirectory:&isdir];
   if (isdir) return YES;
-  if ( fl_filename_match([filename fileSystemRepresentation], filter_pattern[([nspopup indexOfSelectedItem])]) ) return YES;
+  const char *fsname = [filename fileSystemRepresentation];
+  const char *pattern = filter_pattern[selected];
+  if (fsname == NULL || pattern == NULL) return YES;
+  if ( fl_filename_match(fsname, pattern) ) return YES;
   return NO;
 }
 - (BOOL)panel:(id)sender shouldEnableURL:(NSURL *)url
